  "details": "<p>This archive is located in a private house in Assur.</p>\r\n<p><img class=\"image-inline external-image\" height=\"731\" src=\"http://oracc.ub.uni-muenchen.de/atae/images/Plan62_AssurPlan.png\" width=\"534\" /></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "In a private house in Assur, cut into by the excavation trench eD10I, researchers found eight clay tablets and a stamp seal. One of the texts can be dated to 717 BC. The group of texts mostly includes school tablets, as well as a purchase document and an incantation in the form of a letter, written in Babylonian script.",
